# Run after `abort-script` with the same `--state`: the restore runs first
# and the requests below wait for it. The file's buffer comes back with the
# text typed before the abort, modified, in the window, with the cursor the
# last index recorded. Once restored, the session index changes and its
# write waits on the clock: `indexed` moves the clock past
# each write as it comes and waits for every job, so the lines below are in
# one order.
settle
indexed
show
scene
